        <p n="1" ana="#tr.print">The framed manuscript page number [ⲕⲋ] is printed with a bar above and below as the frame, not as a supralinear stroke. An enlarged ϫ begins ϫⲉ after the dots. Measured strokes over the first ⲙ of ⲙⲙ (682–696) and over ⲛ of ⲛⲧϩⲉ (917–929).</p>
        <p n="2" ana="#tr.reading">The ⲓ of ⲧⲉⲓ̈ carries both a diaeresis and a sublinear dot (separate blobs above and below).</p>
        <p n="3" ana="#tr.reading">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲧ. The ϣ of ⲛⲟⲩϣ[ⲏ] has a separate sublinear dot in its lower bowl (8× zoom; the ϣ of ⲛⲟⲩϣⲏ in l. 2 has none); so also ϣ of ⲛⲧϣ[ⲁⲣⲡ] in l. 5. All other ϣ on the page were checked at 5× and carry no dot.</p>
        <p n="7" ana="#tr.bracket">The edition opens a bracket after ⲧⲉ at the line end and never closes it or restores anything; encoded as a loss of uncounted extent.</p>
        <p n="9" ana="#tr.bracket">The bracket opened before the last three dots is not closed in the edition; it is closed here at the line end. So also ll. 12, 31, 32 and 34.</p>
        <p n="10" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke over ⲙⲛ (955–976): ⲙ 52 %, ⲛ 57 %, encoded on both.</p>
        <p n="11" ana="#tr.layout">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲧ.</p>
        <p n="13" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke over ϩⲛ of ⲉⲧϩⲛ (914–934): ϩ 38 %, ⲛ 60 %; encoded on ⲛ only.</p>
        <p n="15" ana="#tr.print">Measured strokes over the two ⲙⲛ: the first (524–545) covers ⲙ 52 %, ⲛ 56 % (encoded on both); the second (1189–1208) covers ⲙ 43 %, ⲛ 53 % (encoded on ⲛ only).</p>
        <p n="17" ana="#tr.print">Two separate strokes in ⲙⲡⲛⲁ: over ⲙ (1046–1059) and over ⲡⲛⲁ (1067–1112; ⲁ 59 %).</p>
        <p n="20" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke over ⲙⲛ (622–642): ⲙ 50 %, ⲛ 53 %, encoded on both.</p>
        <p n="23" ana="#tr.print">The third of the six dots inside the brackets (x 1105) is faint (area 4, below the detector's threshold) but clear in both overlapping 4× strips.</p>
        <p n="28" ana="#tr.layout">Line in ekthesis with an enlarged ⲧ.</p>
        <p n="29" ana="#tr.print">Measured stroke over ⲣ of ⲁⲩϭⲱⲣϭ (645–657). The stroke over ⲥ of ⲁⲩⲛⲧⲥ is printed obliquely.</p>
        <p n="30" ana="#tr.print">The stroke over ϩ of ⲉⲧⲁⲛϩ is printed obliquely. Measured overline over ⲡⲛⲁ of ⲡⲡⲛⲁ (617–662): second ⲡ 84 %, ⲛ 100 %, ⲁ 58 %; not over the first ⲡ.</p>
        <p n="33" ana="#tr.layout">An enlarged ⲧ begins ⲧⲙⲁϩϣⲁⲙⲧ[ⲉ] after the editors' "leer".</p>
      </div>
